      "username": "WalkingTarget",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/walkingtarget/{size}/4833_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-03-05T21:05:54.409Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Tangential connection at best.</p>\n<p><em>FotEG</em> obviously takes place in a setting in which the Lovecraft mythos is a thing.</p>\n<p>We know that the world of Sentinel Comics does not contain the Lovecraft mythos as canonically true. The works of HPL exist here in the real world and within the “metaverse” in which Sentinel Comics is a publishing company. It’s possible that <em>FotEG</em> could be a game that exists in the metaverse. Because the writers of Sentinel Comics can be aware of HPL, it’s also possible for the works of HPL to exist <em>as fiction</em> within the comics as well and so <em>FotEG</em> could be a boardgame within the comics universe too.</p>\n<p>Short version: the events within the game of <em>FotEG</em> could not be “real” in any Sentinels-related property, but the game itself <em>could</em> exist.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-03-05T21:05:54.409Z",
